sometimes we have a concept (like sendMessage)
that have different forms (like normal, urgent, secret,..)
that probably we have some abstract class or interface for them.

each form have some different implementations!
like we can use telegram, email, whatsApp, sms,...
to send each form of message,
it's create a complex hierarchy!

if we want to implement this by "INHERITANCE"
we have n*n situations
(we should implement all abstract classes for telegram, sms, ...)



imagine we have designing a universal remote control app fo TVs,
we have some forms like remote just have base functions (turn on/ turn off)
                   like remote have some advance functions too (select chanel)
simultaneously we need implement these logics separately for each brands (like sony)
now we implement it by "INHERITANCE"


problem: if we want to support another brand like samsung
         we should implement all the hierarchy for samsung!
         we can use bridge pattern to simplify this!